backportcore.settings.family.trickytrialsbackport=Tricky Trials
backportcore.settings.family.trickytrialsbackport.about=1.21's trial chambers, the breeze, the mace, the crafter, copper blocks and the pale garden.
config.backportcore.textures.tooltip=Vanilla's textures as the newest installed backport's version has them.
backportcore.general.textures.moderntextures.tooltip=Give vanilla's blocks, items and mobs the textures of the newest installed backport's version: 1.14's Texture Update to begin with, then every later version's retextures up to that one, such as 1.17's ores with Caves & Cliffs Backport. Off keeps 1.12.2's, and also puts back 1.12.2's look for the backports' own copies of things 1.12.2 already had (the tuxedo, red and Siamese cats).\n\nClient only; a server ignores it. Resource packs you pick, and other mods that change a vanilla texture on purpose, still win over it. Villagers, horses and water keep 1.12.2's textures either way, and a texture a later version redrew for a new model keeps its older look: those don't fit 1.12.2's models or colors.\n\nChanging it in game reloads resources, as F3+T does.
config.backportcore.presentation.tooltip=The parts of the game's look that follow the newest installed backport, as vanilla's did at that version.
backportcore.general.presentation.panorama.tooltip=Which panorama the title screen shows behind its buttons:\nLATEST - the newest installed backport's (vanilla's choice),\na version, such as 1.14 - that version's, if a backport of it is installed (1.12.2 for 1.12.2's own),\nROTATE - a different installed version's each time the game starts.\n\nClient only; a server ignores it. Takes effect the next time the game starts.
backportcore.general.presentation.reportbugslink.tooltip=Where the pause menu's Report Bugs button goes. By default, the backports' Discord. A modpack can point it at its own page. Leave it empty to hide the button.\n\nClient only; a server ignores it.
config.backportcore.lookAndFeel.tooltip=The newer look and feel the installed backports bring, part by part. Also on the Look & Feel page.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.newerlook.tooltip=Use the newer look and feel the installed backports bring. Off: everything below looks and feels as 1.12.2, and each switch keeps its own choice for when this is on again.\n\nClient only; a server ignores it.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.newestlook.tooltip=The newest version whose look is used: Latest (the newest installed backport), or a version such as 1.16 to stop there even with later backports installed.\n\nClient only; a server ignores it.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.loadingscreens.tooltip=The newer world-loading screens: the spawn-area percentage, the chunk grid, the panorama behind it. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.startupscreen.tooltip=The Mojang Studios screen when resources load. Off: none, as 1.12.2.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.titlescreen.tooltip=The newer title screen: panorama, logo, fade-in and Accessibility button. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.splashes.tooltip=The newer versions' splash texts. Off: 1.12.2's list.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.menus.tooltip=Newer menus and buttons: backgrounds, button text, the pause and death screens, world backups. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.optionsscreens.tooltip=The newer options screens (Accessibility, Mouse, Controls, Key Binds) and the options on them. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.videosettings.tooltip=The newer Video Settings: layout, sections, preset and its options. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.chat.tooltip=Command suggestions and the newer chat options. Off: 1.12.2's Tab completion and chat.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.debug.tooltip=The newer F3 screen, F3 keys, Debug Options and charts. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.toasts.tooltip=The music toast and the newer toast textures. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.inventory.tooltip=The creative order, slot highlights and newer container textures. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.music.tooltip=The newer menu music, in-game music and music options. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.sky.tooltip=Each version's fog, sky, clouds and sunrise. Off: 1.12.2's.
backportcore.general.lookandfeel.wording.tooltip=Vanilla's text as the newer versions word it. Off: 1.12.2's wording.
config.backportcore.rendering.tooltip=How the world's chunks are rebuilt when blocks change, as later versions do it.
backportcore.general.rendering.blockupdates.tooltip=Which changed chunks the game rebuilds at once, holding up the frame, instead of on the chunk builder threads. Current vanilla's "Chunk Builder" video setting (1.18.2 on):\nNONE - none; every rebuild is threaded ("Threaded", current vanilla's default; a block\nyou break can leave a hole for a frame),\nPLAYER_AFFECTED - only chunks you changed yourself, by placing or breaking a block\n("Semi Blocking"),\nNEARBY - also every changed chunk within about 28 blocks of the camera ("Fully Blocking",\nthe only rule before 1.18.2). Blocks the server changes nearby, such as a kelp or sugar\ncane column breaking, then cost a rebuild on the render thread every tick.\n\nClient only; a server ignores it. Takes effect at once. OptiFine, Celeritas, Vintagium and Nothirium replace this part of the game with their own threaded rebuilds; with them it does nothing.
config.backportcore.recipes.tooltip=The backports' crafting recipes in the recipe book, unlocked the way vanilla unlocks its own.
backportcore.general.recipes.unlockrecipes.tooltip=Unlock the backports' crafting recipes the way vanilla unlocks its own: holding an iron ingot gives the smithing table's recipe, a stick or coal the campfire's. The recipe toast shows and the recipe appears in the recipe book. Off: the recipes still craft but never show in the recipe book.\n\nRecipes already unlocked stay unlocked.
